== 4.7 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Price elasticity of demand measures],
  [the responsiveness of supply to a change in price],
  [the change in price caused by a change in quantity],
  [the responsiveness of quantity demanded to a change in price],
  [the total revenue earned at each price]
)

#mcq(2, [The price of a good falls from ₦10 to ₦8 and quantity demanded rises from 40 to 60 units. The price elasticity of demand is],
  [0.4],
  [2.5],
  [2.0],
  [0.5]
)

#mcq(3, [A 10% rise in price reduces quantity demanded by 10%. Demand is],
  [unit elastic],
  [elastic],
  [perfectly inelastic],
  [inelastic]
)

#mcq(4, [If the price elasticity of demand for a good is 0.4, demand is],
  [perfectly elastic],
  [elastic],
  [unit elastic],
  [inelastic]
)

#mcq(5, [Demand is said to be perfectly inelastic when the demand curve is],
  [upward-sloping],
  [downward-sloping at 45 degrees],
  [vertical],
  [horizontal]
)

#mcq(6, [Demand is perfectly elastic when the demand curve is],
  [upward-sloping],
  [steeply downward-sloping],
  [horizontal],
  [vertical]
)

#mcq(7, [If demand for a good is elastic, a fall in its price will],
  [leave total revenue unchanged],
  [increase total revenue],
  [reduce quantity demanded],
  [reduce total revenue]
)

#mcq(8, [If demand for a good is inelastic, a rise in its price will],
  [increase total revenue],
  [increase quantity demanded],
  [leave total revenue unchanged],
  [reduce total revenue]
)

#mcq(9, [Total revenue is at its maximum when price elasticity of demand is],
  [infinite],
  [greater than one],
  [one],
  [zero]
)

#mcq(10, [A farmer whose harvest is unusually large may earn less because],
  [the demand for the crop is elastic],
  [the demand for the crop is inelastic],
  [supply has fallen],
  [the government controls prices]
)

#mcq(11, [Which of the following goods is likely to have the most elastic demand?],
  [petrol in the short run],
  [household electricity],
  [salt],
  [a particular brand of soft drink]
)

#mcq(12, [The demand for a necessity is generally],
  [elastic],
  [perfectly elastic],
  [unit elastic],
  [inelastic]
)

#mcq(13, [Demand becomes more elastic in the long run because],
  [incomes always rise],
  [consumers can find substitutes and change their habits],
  [prices are lower in the long run],
  [the government intervenes]
)

#mcq(14, [The elasticity of demand for a good that takes a large share of a consumer's income is likely to be],
  [high],
  [low],
  [negative],
  [zero]
)

#mcq(15, [Price elasticity of supply measures the responsiveness of],
  [quantity supplied to a change in price],
  [supply to a change in income],
  [quantity demanded to a change in price],
  [price to a change in cost]
)

#mcq(16, [The supply of land in a city is],
  [unit elastic],
  [perfectly inelastic],
  [elastic in the short run],
  [perfectly elastic]
)

#mcq(17, [Supply is likely to be more elastic when],
  [there is only one seller],
  [the good is perishable],
  [the firm has spare capacity],
  [the period is very short]
)

#mcq(18, [When consumers' income rises by 10% and quantity demanded rises by 5%, income elasticity is],
  [0.5 and the good is a luxury],
  [2.0 and the good is inferior],
  [2.0 and the good is a luxury],
  [0.5 and the good is a normal necessity]
)

#mcq(19, [A negative income elasticity of demand indicates],
  [a complementary good],
  [a luxury good],
  [an inferior good],
  [a normal good]
)

#mcq(20, [When the price of good A rises and the quantity demanded of good B rises, the cross elasticity is],
  [negative and the goods are substitutes],
  [positive and the goods are substitutes],
  [zero and the goods are unrelated],
  [positive and the goods are complements]
)

#mcq(21, [A negative cross elasticity of demand between two goods means that they are],
  [complements],
  [inferior goods],
  [unrelated],
  [substitutes]
)

#mcq(22, [A cross elasticity of zero between two goods means that they are],
  [complements],
  [the same good],
  [unrelated],
  [substitutes]
)

#mcq(23, [If the cross elasticity between tea and coffee is +1.2, the goods are],
  [substitutes, because the figure is positive],
  [complements, because the figure exceeds one],
  [unrelated],
  [complements, because the figure is positive]
)

#mcq(24, [The burden of a tax on a commodity falls mainly on],
  [the government],
  [the side of the market that is more elastic],
  [the side of the market that is less elastic],
  [the side that hands the money over]
)

#mcq(25, [A government wants to raise revenue with the least reduction in consumption. It should tax a good whose demand is],
  [elastic],
  [inelastic],
  [unit elastic],
  [perfectly elastic]
)

#mcq(26, [A 20% fall in price leads to a 30% rise in quantity demanded. Total revenue will],
  [remain unchanged],
  [rise, because demand is elastic],
  [fall, because price fell],
  [rise, because demand is inelastic]
)

#mcq(27, [Elasticity along a straight-line downward-sloping demand curve],
  [is constant at every point],
  [rises as price falls],
  [is always equal to one],
  [falls from infinity at the price axis to zero at the quantity axis]
)

#mcq(28, [If the demand curve for a good is unit elastic throughout, a fall in price will],
  [increase total revenue],
  [reduce total revenue],
  [leave total revenue unchanged],
  [reduce quantity demanded]
)

#mcq(29, [Which pair of goods is most likely to have a negative cross elasticity of demand?],
  [Coca-Cola and Pepsi],
  [cars and petrol],
  [tea and coffee],
  [butter and margarine]
)

#mcq(30, [The elasticity of demand for a good with many close substitutes is],
  [low],
  [zero],
  [high],
  [negative]
)

#mcq(31, [The short-run supply of agricultural produce is generally],
  [more elastic than in the long run],
  [perfectly elastic],
  [less elastic than in the long run],
  [unrelated to price]
)

#mcq(32, [A firm's total revenue rises when it cuts its price. This shows that demand for its product is],
  [elastic],
  [unit elastic],
  [perfectly inelastic],
  [inelastic]
)

#mcq(33, [If a 5% rise in price reduces quantity demanded by 2%, the price elasticity of demand is],
  [0.4],
  [2.5],
  [0.25],
  [5.0]
)

#mcq(34, [The demand for a good is elastic. A producer wishing to increase total revenue should],
  [reduce output without changing price],
  [lower the price],
  [raise the price],
  [leave the price unchanged]
)

#mcq(35, [Two goods have a cross elasticity of −0.8. A rise in the price of the first will cause the demand for the second to],
  [become perfectly inelastic],
  [rise],
  [stay the same],
  [fall]
)

#mcq(36, [Income elasticity of demand for a luxury good is],
  [between zero and one],
  [negative],
  [exactly zero],
  [greater than one]
)

#mcq(37, [The main determinant of the price elasticity of supply is],
  [the income of buyers],
  [the number of consumers],
  [the price of substitutes],
  [time, together with the availability of spare capacity]
)

#mcq(38, [A good whose price rises by 10% and whose quantity demanded falls by 25% has an elasticity of],
  [2.5],
  [25],
  [0.4],
  [1.0]
)

#mcq(39, [Which statement about elasticity is correct?],
  [elasticity is measured in naira],
  [elasticity is the same as the slope of the demand curve],
  [elasticity compares percentage changes, while slope compares absolute changes],
  [a steep curve is always elastic]
)

#mcq(40, [If the price elasticity of supply of a good is 0.3, its supply is],
  [perfectly elastic],
  [inelastic],
  [elastic],
  [unit elastic]
)

